WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.686
Digital identity infrastructure.

00:00:02.636 --> 00:00:05.227
From ArriveCAN to digital I.D.

00:00:05.227 --> 00:00:13.045
The Known Traveller Digital Identity program was co-sponsored by the Government of Canada, the Government of the Netherlands, and the World Economic Forum.

00:00:13.045 --> 00:00:17.625
It tested blockchain-based digital travel credentials on Air Canada routes.

00:00:17.625 --> 00:00:26.670
ArriveCAN cost fifty-nine million dollars for what was supposed to be an eighty-thousand-dollar app — and created mandatory digital credential infrastructure for border crossing.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:34.488
Treasury Board's Digital Ambition twenty twenty-two document cites WEF frameworks as reference architecture for Canada's digital strategy.

00:00:34.488 --> 00:00:38.397
The pandemic required rapid digital infrastructure deployment.

00:00:38.397 --> 00:00:42.261
That infrastructure did not disappear when the pandemic ended.

00:00:42.261 --> 00:00:50.886
The digital identity systems built during the emergency are now permanent infrastructure — and the WEF frameworks that inspired them continue to evolve.

00:00:50.886 --> 00:00:57.056
This page documents the documented path from pandemic response to permanent digital surveillance infrastructure.

00:00:57.056 --> 00:01:03.852
Three documented digital identity programs that connect Canada's government to WEF digital identity frameworks.

00:01:03.852 --> 00:01:07.988
Three documented concerns about digital identity infrastructure.

00:01:07.988 --> 00:01:10.920
The digital layer of institutional capture.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:20.363
Digital identity infrastructure is the technology layer that connects the surveillance capabilities of the national security state to the institutional control documented across this site.

00:01:20.363 --> 00:01:23.397
CSIS conducts intelligence operations.

00:01:23.397 --> 00:01:26.704
The police enforce with militarized capabilities.

00:01:26.704 --> 00:01:29.613
The Emergencies Act freezes accounts.

00:01:29.613 --> 00:01:36.829
Digital identity infrastructure provides the technical platform that makes all of these capabilities scalable, automated, and permanent.

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:40.034
When identity is digital, control is digital.

00:01:40.034 --> 00:01:48.545
Access to government services, financial transactions, travel, and employment can all be conditioned on digital credentials controlled by captured institutions.

00:01:48.545 --> 00:01:50.772
This is not hypothetical.

00:01:50.772 --> 00:01:53.295
ArriveCAN demonstrated the model.

00:01:53.295 --> 00:01:56.159
KTDI documented the framework.

00:01:56.159 --> 00:01:58.897
Treasury Board adopted the architecture.

00:01:58.897 --> 00:02:01.261
The infrastructure exists.

00:02:01.261 --> 00:02:04.897
The question is how it will be used — and who will control it.
